    'd references stay silent because the compiler reports them with other codes, and so does @Routine (an untyped pointer). Quick fix: move the routine in front of the enclosing routine as a routine of th' +
    'e unit, if it uses nothing from it (no local names further out, no class members without a prefix).",',
    '      "bad": "procedure TListe.Sortieren;\n  function Vergleich(A, B: Pointer): Integer;\n  begin\n    Result := 0;\n  end;\nbegin\n  FListe.Sort(Vergleich);\nend;",',
    '      "good": "function Vergleich(A, B: Pointer): Integer;\nbegin\n  Result := 0;\nend;\n\nprocedure TListe.Sortieren;\nbegin\n  FListe.Sort(Vergleich);\nend;",',
    '      "compilerCodes": [',
